from pathlib import Path
from PIL import Image
import numpy as np,json
from scipy.ndimage import gaussian_filter
R=Path('/PATH/TO/transmissions-from-alpha-centauri');O=R/'art/reviews/surface-056'
refs=R/'references/user-pipe-surface-study'
rois={'reference':{'panel':(810,420,1010,620),'pipe':(135,425,230,690)},'render':{'panel':(620,480,920,780),'pipe':(205,455,260,675)}}
metrics={}
for name in ['reference','clean','mottled','weathered']:
 im=Image.open(refs/'pipe-detail-fine-geometry-and-weathering.png' if name=='reference' else O/(name+'.png')).convert('RGB');metrics[name]={}
 for part,box in rois['reference' if name=='reference' else 'render'].items():
  c=im.crop(box);width=256 if part=='panel' else 128;c=c.resize((width,round(c.height*width/c.width)),Image.Resampling.LANCZOS);c.save(O/f'{name}-{part}.png')
  x=np.asarray(c,dtype=float)/255;y=x@np.array([.2126,.7152,.0722]);energies=[]
  for a,b in [(1,4),(4,12),(12,32)]:
   band=gaussian_filter(y,a)-gaussian_filter(y,b);energies.append(round(float(np.sqrt(np.mean(band**2))*255),3))
  metrics[name][part]={'fine_medium_coarse_RMS_srgb_levels':energies,'roi':box,'normalized_width':width}
(O/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps({'method':'RMS of differences between Gaussian blurs at sigma 1–4, 4–12, 12–32 pixels on normalized-width interior crops. Display-referred luma, not physical luminance. No silhouette, joint or bolt edges. Different shape/lighting/resolution means directional diagnostic only, not a similarity score. Pipe excludes highlight.','data':metrics},indent=2))
review={'status':'awaiting user review','scope':'Isolated native material proof; alley 055 unchanged','findings':['Connected tonal islands now occupy surface interiors and modulate the highlight.','Panel treatment is quieter than pipe treatment.','Full treatment adds existing runoff and scars, but their distribution still reads more scattered than UP-03.','Reference contains stronger directional tonal regions and more deliberate quiet versus worn clusters.'],'subjective_scores_not_measurements':{'interior_coverage':82,'scale_hierarchy':76,'highlight_integration':80,'wear_clustering':70,'form_readability':84},'next':'Tune clusters/quiet areas on a real service assembly, then verify at alley camera scale. Do not interpret texture energy as artistic similarity.'}
(O/'review.json').write_text(json.dumps(review,indent=2))
url='/art/reviews/surface-056/'
def figure(src,title):return f'<figure><a href="{src}"><img loading="lazy" src="{src}" alt="{title}"></a><figcaption>{title}</figcaption></figure>'
stages=''.join(figure(url+n+'.png',t) for n,t in [('clean','A · Clean shading'),('mottled','B · Connected tonal islands'),('weathered','C · Islands + scars and runoff')])
refimgs=''.join(figure('/references/user-pipe-surface-study/'+n,t) for n,t in [('pipe-detail-base-geometry.png','UP-02 · Supplied clean illustration'),('pipe-detail-fine-geometry-and-weathering.png','UP-03 · Supplied detail target')])
crops=''
for part in ['panel','pipe']:
 crops+=f'<h3>{part.title()} interiors</h3><div class="four">'+''.join(figure(url+n+'-'+part+'.png',n.title()) for n in ['reference','clean','mottled','weathered'])+'</div>'
rows=''.join('<tr><td>'+n.title()+'</td><td>'+p+'</td>'+''.join(f'<td>{v:.2f}</td>' for v in metrics[n][p]['fine_medium_coarse_RMS_srgb_levels'])+'</tr>' for p in ['panel','pipe'] for n in metrics)
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>056 · Surface interiors</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#19191e;color:#e5e3e1;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:36px}h1{font-size:38px;margin:10px 0}h2{margin-top:56px}p{max-width:850px;color:#bdbbc4}a{color:#aebcdb}button{background:#373540;color:white;border:1px solid #686574;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 16px;cursor:pointer;position:sticky;top:10px;z-index:2}.three,.two,.four{display:grid;gap:18px;align-items:start}.three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.two{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);max-width:1000px}.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}figure{margin:0;background:#24242b}img{width:100%;display:block}figcaption{padding:12px;color:#ccc}body.gray img{filter:grayscale(1)}.four img{height:360px;object-fit:contain;background:#222228}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:min(100%,850px)}td,th{text-align:left;padding:9px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #393840}small{color:#bbb}@media(max-width:800px){.three,.two{grid-template-columns:1fr}.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}main{padding:18px}}</style><main><a href="/prototype/review-055.html">← Alley checkpoint 055</a><h1>056 · Texture inside the surfaces</h1><p>One bent pipe, one flat panel. Identical geometry and camera across all three native Blender renders. The material fills surface interiors with connected, nested tonal patches, including the pale highlight strip.</p><button onclick="document.body.classList.toggle('gray');this.setAttribute('aria-pressed',document.body.classList.contains('gray'))" aria-pressed="false">Toggle grayscale</button><h2>Three stages</h2>'''+f'<div class="three">{stages}</div>'+'''<p>Click any image for full resolution. C layers the existing scars and runoff over B. The pipe uses separate service wear; facade runoff is confined to the panel. This proof does not change the alley.</p><h2>What improved—and what still misses</h2><p>The smooth interiors now carry related tonal islands at several scales, and the highlight is textured rather than pasted over them. The remaining gap is distribution: UP-03 has more deliberate worn clusters, directional patches and quiet areas. C still carries some scattered dark marks inherited from the earlier treatment.</p><h2>Supplied study</h2>'''+f'<div class="two">{refimgs}</div>'+'''<p>These are user-supplied reference illustrations, not native Blender outputs. Originals and provenance notes are saved in the project reference folder.</p><h2>Interior-only comparison</h2><p>Crops exclude silhouettes, collars and bolts. Panel widths are normalized to 256 pixels and pipe widths to 128; aspect ratio is preserved. The pipe crops exclude the bright highlight. Different framing and source detail limit direct numerical comparison.</p>'''+crops+'''<h2>Texture energy by scale</h2><p>RMS differences between blurred images, measured in 0–255 display-luma levels. Fine: 1–4 px; medium: 4–12 px; coarse: 12–32 px. Higher is not automatically better: these numbers diagnose missing or excessive variation, not artistic similarity.</p><table><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Surface</th><th>Fine</th><th>Medium</th><th>Coarse</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table><h2>Editable proof</h2><p>'''+ ' · '.join(f'<a href="{url}{n}.blend">{n.title()} scene</a>' for n in ['clean','mottled','weathered'])+f' · <a href="{url}connected-tonal-islands.blend">Reusable material group</a>'+'''</p><p>Review status: awaiting your judgment. Next suggested test: clustered tonal wear on an actual service assembly, checked both close up and at the alley camera scale.</p></main></html>'''
(R/'prototype/surface-study-056.html').write_text(html)
print(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2));print((O/'geometry-check.json').read_text())
